// Research checked 2 November 2026. Sources are linked in each skill note.
window.CODEX_SKILLS = [{"id":"attack","name":"Attack","category":"Combat","icon":"swords","summary":"Train the skill, not your downtime. Build around sustained area damage.","bonus":"Sacrifice: +50% combat XP","tiers":{"low":["Laniakea’s spear","Bandos power armour","Attack-only XP selection"],"medium":["Noxious scythe","Augmented Masterwork","Practical damage perks"],"high":["Halberd-range AoE weapon","Vestments of Havoc","Premium damage perks"]},"caution":"Loot sacrificed with XP scrimshaw","notes":"<p>Attack now has a real <strong>120 cap</strong> following the 2 March 2026 combat update. At 99 you can already equip the training weapons below. Set combat XP allocation to <strong>Attack only</strong>: splitting it with Strength/Defence slows this particular goal without increasing total monster XP. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Combat_Style_Modernisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modernisation</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Attack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attack</a></p>\n<p><strong>Direct XP boosts:</strong> Scrimshaw of sacrifice gives <strong>+50% combat XP</strong>, but sacrifices monster drops; it occupies your pocket slot, replacing a damage scripture or vampyrism scrimshaw. During Double XP, its documented combat result is <strong>250% of ordinary base XP</strong>, not 300%. Therefore this is best for pure XP, not the user&#x27;s money-making goal. Melee brawling gloves grant <strong>+50% Attack XP</strong> while charges last, but do <strong>not</strong> work while Double XP is active. Maximum-potency torstol incense supplies a <strong>2% multiplicative XP increase</strong>. Check the XP calculator for other owned boosts; do not simply multiply every percentage. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves_%28Melee%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gloves</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Torstol_incense_sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Torstol</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Calculator:Experience_Buffs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stack calculator</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget</th><th>Training equipment</th><th>Why</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Augmented Laniakea&#x27;s spear (82 Attack), Bandos power armour</td><td>Halberd reach; particularly effective against poisonable low-defence mobs. Its lower accuracy matters against stronger targets.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Augmented noxious scythe (90 Attack), augmented T90 Masterwork</td><td>Better accuracy with halberd reach; power armour and survival for sustained AoE killing.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Noxious scythe for clustered mobs; Vestments of Havoc (95 Defence), Cinderbanes on poisonable targets; appropriate high-end damage perks</td><td>Higher kill throughput. Expensive single-target weapons are not automatically better XP equipment than a halberd.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Noxious_scythe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Scythe and spear comparison</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_melee_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training equipment</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Vestments_of_havoc_armour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vestments</a></p>\n<p>These equipment upgrades boost <strong>kills/hour, not XP per kill</strong>. Overloads, appropriate prayers, aggression supplies and survival also improve uptime. At all-99 Slayer, start with accessible dense mobs rather than recommending 105-Slayer abyssal beasts unconditionally. Benchmark an hour with actual XP and supply costs.</p>\n<p><strong>Obsolete advice:</strong> functional auras and the aura slot were removed on 13 April 2026; do not budget for Berserker or vampyrism auras. Some effects moved elsewhere. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Aura_Overhaul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aura overhaul</a></p>\n<p><strong>Upcoming availability change:</strong> combat dummies and pulse/cinder cores should not be treated as permanent training supplies: MTX item changes are scheduled for <strong>23 November 2026</strong>, after this research date. Check the official transition details before spending on expiring training resources. <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/whats-happening-with-mtx-items-in-runescape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jagex MTX item changes</a></p>\n<p><strong>Uncertainty:</strong> no current live gear prices or universal best XP/hour measured. Several wiki pages retain older combat-era rankings; the scythe recommendation is specifically for reach and AoE, not an assertion that it is the strongest current bossing weapon. No claimed combined multiplier beyond the explicitly documented DXP/sacrifice interaction.</p>"},{"id":"strength","name":"Strength","category":"Combat","icon":"fist","summary":"Reach more targets. Keep your damage, healing and training rhythm in balance.","bonus":"Melee brawlers: +50–75%","tiers":{"low":["Laniakea’s spear","Bandos power armour","Strength-only XP selection"],"medium":["Noxious scythe","Augmented Masterwork","Cinderbanes on eligible mobs"],"high":["Tumeken’s Light","High-end power armour","Optimised AoE perks"]},"caution":"Brawlers do not work with DXP","notes":"<p>Strength now has a <strong>real level-120 cap</strong>. Select <strong>Strength only</strong> under Combat XP to concentrate melee XP there; selecting Attack/Strength/Defence splits the award rather than multiplying it. Constitution XP remains separate. The 2026 modernisation moved Strength abilities into the Attack ability book. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Strength\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Strength</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Combat_Style_Modernisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modernisation</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget</th><th>Training equipment</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Augmented <strong>Laniakea’s spear</strong>, Bandos power armour, owned combat jewellery; basic damage perks</td><td>Halberd reach improves clustered-monster clearing. Spear’s poison synergy is target-dependent; verify accuracy.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td><strong>Noxious scythe</strong>, augmented Masterwork body/legs, Cinderbanes on poisonable enemies, improved damage perks</td><td>Higher accuracy and survivability support consistent unattended area damage. These are throughput improvements, not XP multipliers.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td><strong>Tumeken’s Light</strong>, optionally Genesis-enchanted T100, strong melee power armour and premium perks</td><td>Its on-kill area-damage passive and halberd range make it the premier area-clearing melee weapon. Not economical solely for training on a 100m budget.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Weapon/Melee_weapons\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Weapon tiers</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Masterwork_armour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Masterwork</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Tumeken%27s_Light\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tumeken’s Light</a></p>\n<p><strong>Direct XP bonuses:</strong> a <strong>scrimshaw of sacrifice gives +50% combat XP</strong> but destroys ordinary drops, including bones; therefore it conflicts with money-making and bonecrusher-based prayer restoration, and occupies the pocket slot instead of a damage scripture. It does not increase augmented-item XP. During Double XP, combat reaches 250% base from those two effects, rather than multiplying to 300%. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice</a></p>\n<p><strong>Melee brawling gloves give +50%, or +75% with tier-4 Infernal Puzzle Box</strong>, consume charges, and do not work with Double XP. They replace combat gloves. Ignore the older Strength page’s obsolete Wilderness +300% claim; the dedicated glove page supplies the current rule. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves_%28Melee%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Melee gloves</a></p>\n<p><strong>Torstol incense gives up to +2% multiplicatively</strong> at potency four. Eligible Demon Slayer armour provides <strong>+2% combat XP and +4% damage per piece against qualifying demons</strong>, but it is ranged armour: body/legs can hurt melee accuracy, and replacing power armour/perks can reduce XP/hour. Test small slot substitutions rather than wearing the full set. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Torstol_incense_sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Torstol</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Demon_slayer_equipment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Demon Slayer equipment</a></p>\n<p>At all-99, use clustered abyssal demons or another unlocked multi-target population; <strong>abyssal beasts require 105 Slayer</strong>, so label them a later unlock. Aggression, overloads, prayer and sustain increase uptime, not XP per kill. Berserker/Brawler auras are obsolete after 2026 changes. <strong>Uncertainty:</strong> the general melee guide explicitly flags outdated XP data; no defensible current universal XP/hour or fully stacked maximum was established.</p>"},{"id":"defence","name":"Defence","category":"Combat","icon":"shield","summary":"Your damage gear can train Defence. Choose the XP allocation deliberately.","bonus":"Wise 4: capped daily bonus","tiers":{"low":["Owned T90 Necromancy weapons","Deathdealer or Deathwarden","Defence-only XP selection"],"medium":["First Necromancer armour","Zuk cape & Amulet of Souls","Overloads and AoE Revolution"],"high":["Omni guard & Soulbound lantern","Strong damage perks","Reliable sustain"]},"caution":"Constitution XP stays separate","notes":"<p><strong>Best immediate change: select Defence alone in Settings → Gameplay → Combat XP for your chosen style.</strong> Selecting Defence plus Necromancy divides the allocatable XP between them; Defence-only concentrates it without requiring defensive equipment. Constitution still receives its separate allocation. Defence can be trained using any combat style. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Defence_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Defence training</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget tier</th><th>Practical equipment</th><th>What it improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Existing T90 Death guard/Skull lantern; Deathdealer power armour, or Deathwarden where survival limits uptime</td><td>Kill speed and sustained combat, not XP per kill</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium / your existing setup</td><td>Keep First Necromancer armour, T90 weapons, Zuk cape and Amulet of Souls; use suitable overloads, prayer and an AoE Revolution bar</td><td>Your current armour is already ample; improve consistency before buying more</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Omni guard and Soulbound lantern; damage perks and appropriate sustain; retain power armour</td><td>More damage/uptime; benefits vary with monster density and respawns</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>These are a practical Necromancy route for this account, not a claim that Necromancy universally beats every style. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Recommended_equipment_for_PvM/Necromancy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Equipment reference</a></p>\n<p><strong>Direct boosts:</strong> Scrimshaw of sacrifice adds <strong>50% combat XP</strong>, but destroys ordinary loot and occupies the pocket slot, replacing Scripture of Wen or another damage book. Compare actual hourly Defence XP: a book can improve kill speed. During Double XP, the scrimshaw produces <strong>250% combat XP</strong>, rather than multiplying 200% by 150%. It does not boost augmented-item XP. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice</a></p>\n<p>Torstol incense reaches <strong>2% multiplicative XP</strong> at potency four; six sticks overload instantly. Wise 4 adds <strong>4% of base XP</strong>, capped at <strong>50,000 extra XP/day</strong> across all skills, but sacrificing a strong damage perk can reduce overall training speed. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Torstol_incense_sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Torstol</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Wise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wise</a></p>\n<p>Owned combat brawling gloves boost Defence by <strong>50%</strong>, or <strong>75% with tier-four Infernal Puzzle Box</strong>. They work across styles, consume charges, replace combat gloves, and <strong>do not work with active Double XP</strong>. They are untradeable drops, not normal purchases. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brawlers</a></p>\n<p>Inspire Awe provides <strong>2% combat XP</strong>, but its late Archaeology unlock is not assumed for an all-99 account; verify unlock requirements before planning it. Functional auras were removed in April 2026: older Berserker/Vampyrism/Penance aura recommendations are obsolete. No verified universal XP/hour or exact BIS perk set is claimed here. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Aura_Overhaul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aura overhaul</a></p>"},{"id":"ranged","name":"Ranged","category":"Combat","icon":"bow","summary":"Clear clustered enemies with the right ammunition and a sustainable loadout.","bonus":"Sacrifice: +50% combat XP","tiers":{"low":["Affordable augmented bow","Ranged power armour","Ranged-only XP selection"],"medium":["Noxious longbow or equivalent","Pernix power armour","Appropriate damage perks"],"high":["Bow of the Last Guardian","Elite Dracolich armour","Optimised ammunition"]},"caution":"Equipment increases kill throughput","notes":"<p><strong>Priority:</strong> train with dense, rapidly respawning monsters and select <strong>Ranged-only combat XP</strong>. Selecting Defence too divides the style XP between those skills; Constitution is awarded separately. Ranged now has a real 120 cap following March 2026 modernisation. No Ranged skilling outfit provides a conventional permanent 6% training bonus.</p>\n<p><strong>Direct XP boosts:</strong> Scrimshaw of sacrifice grants <strong>+50% combat XP</strong>, but destroys the affected monster loot and occupies the pocket slot. Its superior version lasts longer, rather than adding a bigger percentage. This is a speed purchase, unsuitable for simultaneously rebuilding a weapon fund. Clan Citadel weekly XP buff gives <strong>3–6%</strong> according to fealty. Torstol incense gives up to <strong>2%</strong>, with maximum potency after ramp-up or overloading six sticks. Treat these as individually verified effects, <strong>not a blanket multiplied 1.50 × 1.06 × 1.02 total</strong>: effect stacking is not established by the sources inspected. Do not budget sacrifice as another +50% on top of Double XP without checking that event&#x27;s exclusions.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget</th><th>Equipment and training recommendation</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Existing ranged power armour, inexpensive T80+ weapon, Soul Split/overload support. Mechanised chinchompas plus a strong off-hand are an alternative for tightly packed low-defence enemies; compare ammunition cost and observed kill rate.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Augmented Sirenic or owned Pernix, Noxious longbow/Ascension crossbows, affordable damage perks. Prioritise suitable AoE abilities and uninterrupted aggression before luxury stat upgrades. These increase kills/hour, not XP per kill.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Bow of the Last Guardian, appropriate ammunition, advanced perks and suitable elite Dracolich or T100 Masterwork ranged armour. Masterwork requires level 100; it is not immediately wearable at 99. Choice depends on rotation, enemy defence and sustain; “highest tier” does not prove fastest training.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Method:</strong> Abyssal beasts become available at 105 Slayer; at the user&#x27;s 104, boost or finish 105. Suitable personal Slayer dungeon arrangements reduce competition. Test a 15-minute Revolution run before expensive purchases. Avoid publishing legacy Abyss/chinchompa XP figures: the training page itself warns its rates need revision after the 2023 combat XP changes. Old combat-aura recommendations are obsolete after April 2026&#x27;s overhaul. Dummies, cores and wildcards should be listed separately as temporary/pre-removal systems, not permanent setup recommendations.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Ranged_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ranged training and outdated-rate warning</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Recommended_equipment_for_PvM/Ranged\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">equipment</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Clan_Avatar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">clan buff</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Torstol_incense_sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">torstol</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Aura_Overhaul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aura Overhaul</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic","name":"Magic","category":"Combat","icon":"staff","summary":"Area damage and fewer interruptions make for a stronger training session.","bonus":"Sacrifice: +50% combat XP","tiers":{"low":["Augmented affordable weapon","Subjugation power armour","Suitable multi-target abilities"],"medium":["T90 Magic weapons","Virtus armour","Overloads & damage perks"],"high":["Premium Magic weapons","High-end power armour","Method-specific AoE setup"]},"caution":"Check combat-era guide dates","notes":"<p>Magic now progresses to 120. Equipment increases kills per hour; it does not inherently multiply the XP awarded for each monster. Select <strong>Magic only</strong> in Combat XP settings if the goal is fastest Magic progression: selecting Defence splits the allocated style XP.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget tier</th><th>Training equipment and priorities</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Augmentable T80–87 weapon (chaotic staff if already owned; Obliteration otherwise), Subjugation power armour, existing Amulet of Souls, overloads, Torment and aggression potions. Add Corruption Blast for grouped enemies. Do not buy a premium bossing kit before testing survival and spawn limits.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>T90 weapon such as Legatus’s Emberstaff or upgraded Inquisitor staff <strong>only against susceptible melee-classed targets</strong>; Virtus armour, damage perks, Greater Chain and Caroming 4 for grouped monsters. Unlock Magma Tempest when affordable. AoE unlocks may improve training more than small weapon-tier upgrades.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Roar of Awakening + Ode to Deceit, or content-appropriate Fractured Staff of Armadyl setup; high-end power armour and perks, Greater Chain/Caroming 4, Magma Tempest, Corruption Blast, upgraded damage prayers. Cryptbloom + Animate Dead is a survival alternative, not an XP multiplier, and can sacrifice damage.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Direct XP boosts:</strong> scrimshaw of sacrifice gives +50% combat XP but destroys ordinary loot; occupies the pocket slot and therefore replaces damage books. Magic brawling gloves give +50%, or +75% with tier-4 Infernal Puzzle Box, but are consumable rare drops rather than purchasable permanent equipment. They do not work during active Double XP. Generic boosts include clan bonus up to 6%, torstol incense up to 2%, Inspire Awe 2%, and Wise up to 4% subject to its 50,000 daily bonus-XP cap. Avoid presenting all bonuses as one multiplicative product: stacking categories differ.</p>\n<p><strong>Training:</strong> dense abyssal demons are accessible at 99 Slayer; high-volume grouped combat rewards AoE. Beasts require 105 Slayer, so not an immediate all-99 option. Lunar processing offers noncombat Magic XP but generally trades combat throughput for materials, clicks, and possible profit.</p>\n<p><strong>Current-version cautions:</strong> Maniacal and other functional auras are obsolete after the April 2026 overhaul. Historical XP/hour and Revolution bars may predate March modernisation. Legacy MTX dummies/cores should not anchor a permanent build; planned November removal details require central confirmation. No universal fastest setup established without target, budget and measured kills/hour.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Magic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Magic mechanics</a>; <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Magic_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">XP items and training</a>; <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves_%28Magic%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brawling gloves</a>; <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice scrimshaw</a>; <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Aura_Overhaul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aura overhaul</a>; <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Combat_Style_Modernisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modernisation</a>.</p>"},{"id":"necromancy","name":"Necromancy","category":"Combat","icon":"skull","summary":"Choose active rituals or relaxed combat. Each path needs a different kit.","bonus":"Ritualist outfit: +6% ritual XP","tiers":{"low":["Necromancy cape","Alteration necklace","Best owned Underworld Grimoire"],"medium":["Ritualist’s outfit","Grimoire 3","Wise 4 off-hand for rituals"],"high":["Underworld Grimoire 4","Ring of Kayazu","Optimised attraction layout"]},"caution":"Attraction III requires level 107","notes":"<p><strong>Fastest active route:</strong> City of Um tier-3 rituals, completing every disturbance. <strong>Relaxed route:</strong> sustained multi-target Revolution combat. Damage equipment increases kills/hour; it does not itself multiply awarded XP.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Ritual equipment</th><th>Combat equipment</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Necromancy cape, alteration necklace, best owned Underworld Grimoire; tier-3 ritual and attraction glyphs</td><td>T90 Death guard/Skull lantern, T90 deathdealer, Zuk cape; Salve amulet (e) against undead</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Add full Ritualist’s outfit (+6% ritual XP), Grimoire 3 (+9% disturbance XP), Wise 4 augmented off-hand</td><td>Existing First Necromancer set + T90 weapons; overloads, suitable sustain, damage perks; use existing gear before buying upgrades</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Grimoire 4 (+12% disturbance XP), Ring of Kayazu (+80 percentage points soul attraction; chance to double disturbance rewards), full outfit, cape and necklace</td><td>First Necromancer, Omni guard + Soulbound lantern, Igneous Kal-Mor, appropriate damage perks; expensive upgrades are throughput, not direct XP boosts</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Important mechanics:</strong> alteration necklace strengthens alteration glyphs by 20%. Attraction III requires 107; visible boosts can unlock site glyphs earlier, but the cape’s chosen glyph requires the real level. Attraction influences disturbance quality; simply maximising ritual output with Multiply is not maximising XP. Speed can change disturbance counts, so compare layouts in the ritual calculator rather than assuming maximum Speed wins. Ungael gives 20% less completion AND disturbance XP than Um in exchange for convenience/durability.</p>\n<p><strong>Direct boosts:</strong> maximum-potency torstol incense +2%; Wise 4 +4%, capped at 50,000 bonus XP/day; clan bonus up to6%; Inspire Awe +2% combat-skill XP. Scrimshaw of sacrifice gives +50% monster combat XP but sacrifices loot, conflicting with this account’s money goal. Select Necromancy-only combat XP if training Defence is unnecessary.</p>\n<p><strong>Personal priority:</strong> already-owned First Necromancer/T90/Zuk gear is a strong combat starting point. Buy the cheap ritual necklace and unlock Grimoire rewards before luxury combat equipment. Do not budget around removed functional auras or future MTX changes. Ring double rewards must not be described as automatically doubling XP; exact optimal hourly rates remain layout-, level- and interaction-dependent.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Rituals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rituals</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Underworld_Grimoire\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grimoire</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Necromancy_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">training boosts</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Ungael_ritual_site\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ungael penalty</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sacrifice scrimshaw</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Calculator:Necromancy/Rituals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">calculator</a>.</p>"},{"id":"constitution","name":"Constitution","category":"Combat","icon":"heart","summary":"Train alongside combat. Survival and steady kills keep the XP flowing.","bonus":"Combat brawlers: +50–75%","tiers":{"low":["Owned combat equipment","Appropriate AoE abilities","Reliable sustain"],"medium":["Overloads & damage prayer","Aggression where appropriate","Torstol incense"],"high":["T95 Necromancy weapons","Premium damage perks","A sustained AoE setup"]},"caution":"Beyond 99 is virtual progression","notes":"<p><strong>Constitution remains a level-99 skill: further levels are virtual. Train it alongside another combat skill rather than buying a separate Constitution setup.</strong> Combat awards roughly one Constitution XP per three style XP; changing the selected style/Defence split does not redirect that fixed Constitution share. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">XP allocation</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and approach</th><th>What improves XP</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low additional cost</td><td>Keep your First Necromancer armour, T90 Death guard/Skull lantern, Zuk cape and Amulet of Souls; Revolution AoE against densely packed appropriate monsters</td><td>More kills, reliable survival and less banking; these are throughput improvements, not an XP multiplier</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Add overloads, appropriate damage prayer, aggression potion where monsters permit; Torstol incense at maximum potency</td><td>Torstol gives 2% multiplicative XP. Potion and prayer damage improve kills/hour rather than XP per kill</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>T95 Necromancy weapons and strong AoE damage perks, while retaining sustainable defence; test whether pocket damage beats an XP scrimshaw</td><td>Expensive equipment only helps when it increases sustained kills/hour; do not buy it solely for virtual Constitution levels</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Direct boosters:</strong> available combat brawling gloves boost Constitution by 50%, or 75% with Infernal Puzzle Box tier 4+. The melee version can boost Constitution even while using Necromancy. Charges are limited; DXP disables their bonus; sacrificing your normal gloves also loses equipment benefits. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brawling gloves</a> Maximum-potency <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Torstol_incense_sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Torstol incense</a> multiplies XP by 1.02; a 1.75× brawler bonus combined with it is 1.785× before other boosts.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Wise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wise</a> adds 1% per rank, max 4%, capped at 50,000 bonus XP daily shared across skills. A Wise Excalibur must actually be equipped; carrying it does not help, and replacing your lantern can lose far more combat throughput.</p>\n<p><strong>Caveats:</strong> <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sacrifice scrimshaw</a> advertises +50% combat XP but destroys loot and replaces your damage pocket item; Constitution-specific behaviour was not explicitly confirmed in the retrieved documentation, so its exact HP bonus is unresolved here. Old aura rotations are outdated after the <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Update:Aura_Overhaul_%26_April_Marketplace_Drop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">April 2026 overhaul</a>. Check the shared November 23 transition notes before relying on legacy XP supplies.</p>"},{"id":"prayer","name":"Prayer","category":"Combat","icon":"prayer","summary":"The right burial method matters more than simply buying pricier bones.","bonus":"Burial powder: 3.5× base XP","tiers":{"low":["Owned First Age pieces","Prayer cape","Price-checked bones"],"medium":["Powder of burials","Full First Age outfit","Bank preset & bone hotkey"],"high":["High-XP bones","Owned Prayer brawlers","Infernal Puzzle Box tier 4"]},"caution":"Powder bonus does not multiply with DXP","notes":"<p><strong>Best repeatable speed: bank-side powder-of-burials training.</strong> Prayer is a 99-cap skill; experience beyond 99 gives virtual levels, without new training equipment gates.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and method kit</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low spend</td><td>Dragon bones selected by current GP/XP; existing First Age pieces; Prayer cape; Chaos altar only with the appropriate Wilderness achievement tiers</td><td>Avoid buying premium bones. Chaos altar is 1.5× initially, rising by 0.5× per achievement tier to 3.5× at elite; do not assume everyone receives 3.5×.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Powder of burials, dinosaur/dragonkin/frost-dragon bones after price comparison, full First Age outfit, modified tiara; bank preset and bone hotkey</td><td>Powder gives 3.5× burial XP for 30 minutes. Outfit adds 6%; tiara has a 2% chance to save offerings.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Same powder kit, highest-base-XP bones affordable, Prayer brawling gloves if already owned, tier-4 Infernal Puzzle Box</td><td>Gloves multiply eligible XP by 1.75 with that unlock; their limited charges make high-XP bones especially valuable. They are untradeable, not a normal cash purchase.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/2026_early-game_rebalance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chaos/chapel changes</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Prayer_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">training and saving equipment</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brawling_gloves_%28Prayer%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">brawling glove mechanics</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Stacking:</strong> powder × tier-4 brawlers is <strong>3.5 × 1.75 = 6.125×</strong> before other eligible boosts. Full First Age is not available simultaneously with gloves: replacing its bracelet loses the full-set bonus. Powder does not boost scattered ashes; perfect juju Prayer&#x27;s 5% does not stack with powder. Dragon Rider amulet and auto-sanctifier also do not provide another burial multiplier. Do not multiply this setup by Double XP or knowledge bombs. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Powder_of_burials\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Powder restrictions</a>.</p>\n<p>For bone conservation rather than maximum speed, consider tier-3 Fort chapel with lit burners: 3× base XP after the 2026 reduction, retaining offering-saving benefits. First Age costs 5,000 ecto-tokens plus 1,000 for the tiara upgrade; its XP bonus does not work at Ectofuntus. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/First_age_outfit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Planning:</strong> compare live cost per effective XP, not bone price alone. Do not build a permanent kit around pulse/cinder cores because of the planned November 23 removal; no retired aura assumed. Exact current GP/XP and observed banking throughput remain unverified.</p>"},{"id":"summoning","name":"Summoning","category":"Combat","icon":"summon","summary":"Make your charm stock go further, then remove the banking bottleneck.","bonus":"Summoning focus: +20% base XP","tiers":{"low":["Summoning cape","Owned Shaman pieces","Fast bank preset"],"medium":["Full Shaman outfit","Modified headdress","Spirit gems"],"high":["Summoning focuses","High-XP pouch ingredients","Fast obelisk banking"]},"caution":"Charm saving is not an XP multiplier","notes":"<p><strong>Best investment: Shaman&#x27;s outfit, fast banking, and saved charms before expensive consumable boosts.</strong> Beyond 99, Summoning levels are virtual; there are no higher-level familiars to unlock.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and training setup</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Summoning cape; any owned Shaman pieces; bank preset containing charms, pouches, spirit shards and tertiary ingredients. Make high-XP pouches supported by existing charms. Collect blue/crimson charms with a charming imp rather than destroying them.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full Shaman outfit (+6% XP), modified headdress (5% charm save), spirit gems; Amlodd obelisk with attuned crystal teleport seed, Dive/Double Surge and Mobile for banking.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Same outfit; Taverley shop-unnoting method with magic notepaper or currently available portable deposit box; geyser titans from blue charms. Add Summoning focuses (+20% base XP, one consumed per pouch), torstol incense and Wise 4 if worthwhile.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Summoning_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">training guide</a> benchmarks roughly 15,000 pouches/hour for Taverley versus 5,900/hour with efficient Prifddinas banking. These are execution-dependent, not guaranteed. Do not confuse <strong>Spirit Weaver&#x27;s +50% XP per pouch</strong> with faster training: it changes instant batch creation to one pouch every 2.4 seconds and dramatically reduces throughput.</p>\n<p><strong>Charm saving is not a direct XP multiplier.</strong> Cape saves 2%; spirit onyx saves 60% while charged, improving XP from a finite charm stock. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Spirit_onyx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spirit onyx</a>. Do not add these percentages indiscriminately without confirming the game&#x27;s independent save rolls.</p>\n<p><strong>Stacking:</strong> Amlodd Voice of Seren grants +20% base XP. With focus, their base factors are 1.2 × 1.2 = 1.44; eligible DXP then gives 2.88 times ordinary base XP before other bonuses. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Voice_of_Seren\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Voice</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">XP stacking</a>. This applies at Amlodd, not Taverley. DXP and stored bonus XP can coexist; do not multiply every generic percentage together. Wise is daily-capped. Charm gathering time and tertiary cost must be included in practical efficiency.</p>\n<p><strong>Transition caveat:</strong> portable/core-based legacy guides need rechecking against 23 November MTX changes; focus and spirit gems are retained. No aura recommended. Unknowns: owned charms, outfit pieces, Prifddinas access and current tertiary/focus prices.</p>"},{"id":"archaeology","name":"Archaeology","category":"Gathering","icon":"mattock","summary":"Find artefacts efficiently. Restoration and material supply complete the picture.","bonus":"Archaeologist outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Owned Imcando mattock","Archaeologist outfit","Guild precision upgrades"],"medium":["Mattock of Time and Space","Master archaeologist outfit","Auto-screener & porters"],"high":["Guildmaster Tony’s mattock","Balarak’s sash brush","Tea & precision consumables"]},"caution":"High-end relics require levels above 99","notes":"<p><strong>Priority:</strong> artefact throughput plus restoration, rather than excavation XP alone. Precision progresses artefacts; focus/material-success bonuses supply restoration materials. These are not direct XP multipliers.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Recommended setup at 99</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Elder rune mattock (non-augmentable) or retain an owned augmented Imcando; regular archaeologist outfit (+6% XP); purchase permanent Guild precision upgrades; use signs of the porter.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Augmented Mattock of Time and Space (99, Guildmaster qualification, Plague’s End; crystal + Imcando + shard); master archaeologist outfit with regular set owned (+6% inherited XP and +7% excavation success); Honed 6 plus Fortune/Imp Souled; auto-screener and Grace of the Elves for uptime.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Guildmaster Tony’s mattock (85 base precision vs Time and Space’s 80), Balarak’s sash brush off-hand, cosmic accumulator, waterfiend familiar, hi-spec monocles, material manuals and archaeologist’s tea. Brush rewards following the time sprite, so its value falls when fully AFK.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Boosts:</strong> tea gives +50% excavation XP, not restoration XP. Monocles add 20% base precision; material manuals improve material finding by 10%; master outfit extends these consumables from 20 to 30 minutes. Follow the sprite and restore with the outfit equipped. Honed 6 gives +12% material-success chance, not faster artefact progress. Fortune can duplicate finds; Imp Souled saves porter charges/interruptions. Furnace destroys materials for a relatively small excavation-XP gain and is usually inferior for total training value. New Preservationist combinations should be checked against the current perk page before expensive rolls.</p>\n<p><strong>Above-99 gates:</strong> Flow State (+20% base precision, no soil) requires 102 Archaeology; Inspire Effort (+2% gathering XP) requires 117. Do not present these as unlocked merely because the account has all 99s. DXP doubles base precision rather than restoration XP; do not stockpile restorations expecting double rewards. No obsolete accuracy/skilling aura is required.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Archaeology_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and consumables</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Mattock_of_Time_and_Space\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mattock</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Balarak%27s_sash_brush\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brush</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Optimal_skilling_perk_setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Perks</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Double_XP\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DXP</a>.</p>\n<p>Uncertainty: no quoted GP prices; old cached pages and newly introduced perk combinations need current in-game cost checks. Avoid relying on time-limited MTX cores/replicators in a permanent setup.</p>"},{"id":"divination","name":"Divination","category":"Gathering","icon":"wisp","summary":"Build for your activity: wisp harvesting and Colossi reward different setups.","bonus":"Diviner outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Diviner outfit","Divination urns","Memory-conversion XP setting"],"medium":["Urn enhancer","Pontifex shadow ring","Appropriate familiar"],"high":["Memory dowser for wisps","Divine Conversion relic","Method-specific upgrades"]},"caution":"Dowser is not needed for Colossi","notes":"<p><strong>Priority: investigate the new Colossi activity for active XP; use world 79 incandescent wisps for relaxed energy/XP.</strong> Colossi launched 28 September 2026, requiring 77 Divination and partial Heralds of Crimson. Charge the stone, carry it to murals, deposit; teleports are blocked while carrying it. Route execution is a throughput improvement, not an XP multiplier. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Colossi_Divination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Colossi mechanics</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment/unlocks</th><th>Benefit</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Diviner’s outfit; appropriate Divination urns; 99 cape for wisps; incandescent boon</td><td>Outfit +6% XP; urns approximately +20% of eligible base XP; cape extends springs; boon improves that tier’s conversion XP/energy by 10%.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Elder divination outfit, retaining owned Diviner bonus; urn enhancer; Pontifex observation ring or enriched shadow ring</td><td>Elder outfit improves gathering; enhancer boosts urn payout by 25%, turning nominal 20% into 25%, <strong>not +25% total XP</strong>. Rings give 1% or 3% Divination XP; must be worn for skilling bonus.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Colossi: stonevein amulet, Double Surge, Dive, Mobile/Shadow’s Grace, Scripture of Elidinis. Wisps: memory dowser + Divine Conversion relic (98 Archaeology), enriched ring, boosted gathering setup</td><td>Colossi movement reduces travel; scripture supplies separate XP procs. Dowser automates nearby-rift conversion; Divine Conversion still helps maximise throughput. This is not a universal multiplicative XP bonus.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Divination_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfits, urns, cape, relic</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Memory_dowser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Memory dowser</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pontifex_shadow_ring\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ring rules</a></p>\n<p><strong>Method distinctions:</strong> Hall of Memories/core parties remain an alternative; do not call them fastest without comparing Colossi. Enhanced-XP rift mode consumes energy for 25% more conversion XP; energy mode prioritises money, not XP. Energy-gathering scrimshaws increase resources, not a flat XP percentage; memory-crushing scrimshaw affects conversion. Pocket items conflict with Scripture. Urns and effigies are mutually exclusive. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Energy-gathering_scrimshaw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Scrimshaw</a></p>\n<p><strong>Unknowns:</strong> no independently measured current Colossi maximum verified; do not promise a precise XP/hour. Enrichment auras were removed 13 April 2026 and replaced by level-based passives; exclude aura purchases. Keep limited promotional boosts separate pending November MTX changes. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Divination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Divination updates</a></p>"},{"id":"farming","name":"Farming","category":"Gathering","icon":"leaf","summary":"Plan each run. Yield, animal health and check-health XP are different benefits.","bonus":"Farmer outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Farmer outfit","Magic secateurs","Farming urns"],"medium":["Master farmer outfit","Urn enhancer","Healthy animal management"],"high":["Premium crop & animal plan","Method-specific scrolls","Unlocked high-level supplies"]},"caution":"Animal growth XP has DXP exclusions","notes":"<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and boosts</th><th>Why it helps</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Farmer’s outfit, Farming cape, decorated Farming urns; healthy, happy dragons at Manor Farm</td><td>Outfit gives <strong>6% XP</strong>; urns return <strong>20% of eligible base XP</strong>. Cape has a <strong>5% instant-harvest chance</strong>, a speed benefit rather than extra XP per crop.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Master farmer outfit <strong>with farmer’s outfit owned</strong>, urn enhancer, maximum-potency torstol incense; Wise 4 on an augmented weapon</td><td>Elite outfit inherits the 6%, rather than adding another 6%. Urn enhancer raises the urn return from 20% to <strong>25%</strong>. Torstol adds <strong>2%</strong>; Wise 4 adds <strong>4%</strong>, capped at 50,000 bonus XP/day.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Above, plus banked beans for supreme-growth potions, patch/liquid patch bombs, appropriate Brassica primers, clan 6% and Inspire Effort relic 2%</td><td>Growth potions convert saved beans into rapid patch XP. Teleports and instant harvesting reduce time; no expensive conventional Farming tool is required.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>Equipment figures and growth-potion methods: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Farming_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Farming training</a>. Treat bonuses as additive where applicable, with urn rewards calculated separately—not every listed percentage multiplied together. Expensive time-saving setups are method-dependent.</p>\n<p><strong>Animals:</strong> harvest at full health/happiness; poor condition can reduce XP to 10%. Shiny animals give <strong>25% more XP</strong>. Animal harvests fill urns and accept bonus XP, but <strong>do not receive the Double XP event multiplier</strong>. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Player-owned_farm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Player-owned farm</a></p>\n<p><strong>Yield is not XP:</strong> magic secateurs and ultracompost support profitable, reliable crops; dragon manure makes ultracompost. Juju Farming potions and giant ents add produce without matching XP. Wolpertingers specifically double bush yield <strong>and XP</strong>. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Farming\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Farming</a></p>\n<p><strong>Gates/exclusions:</strong> tombshrooms need <strong>109</strong>, Farming master cape <strong>120</strong>; neither is baseline equipment at 99. No Farming-specific brawling gloves. Dwarven harvester XP mode doubles applicable harvest base XP but forfeits produce and does not work during DXP; limited legacy supply is unsuitable as the permanent baseline. Brassica primer scope differs between overview/training pages: verify the intended patch before spending it. Avoid obsolete aura recommendations after the April 2026 overhaul; do not assume post-November-23 MTX availability.</p>"},{"id":"fishing","name":"Fishing","category":"Gathering","icon":"fish","summary":"Keep casting, catch efficiently, and decide whether to keep or consume the fish.","bonus":"Enhanced decorated urns: 25%","tiers":{"low":["Owned rod & angler outfit","Fishing urns","Suitable familiar"],"medium":["Augmented crystal rod","Fury shark outfit","Urn enhancer"],"high":["Tavia’s fishing rod","Premium method-specific perks","Highest usable urns"]},"caution":"Furnace consumes catches for XP","notes":"<p><strong>Best-value priority:</strong> Fury shark outfit, appropriate augmented tool, Honed/Furnace, urns and perfect juju; Tavia is a luxury purchase. Fishing currently caps at 99, so further levels are virtual, rather than gates to new Fishing equipment. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Fishing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Skill cap</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and consumables</th><th>What improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Fishing outfit; decorated fishing urns; perfect juju fishing potion; granite lobster</td><td>Outfit gives <strong>5% XP</strong>; decorated urns return <strong>20%</strong> of eligible base XP; juju adds <strong>10% catch success</strong>; lobster provides <strong>+4 invisible Fishing</strong> and a listed 3% catch-rate boost.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Fury shark outfit; augmented crystal rod for rod-compatible spots, enhanced rod-o-matic otherwise; Honed 6/Furnace 4; urn enhancer; ring of whispers</td><td>Fury adds <strong>7% success</strong> and <strong>10% double catches with XP</strong>, inherits the owned Fishing outfit bonus, and can consume fish to avoid banking. Crystal rod adds <strong>8% success</strong>, enhanced rod-o-matic <strong>4%</strong>.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Augmented Tavia&#x27;s rod at compatible spots; level-20 tool; optimal combined perks; exquisite urns if owned</td><td>Tavia adds <strong>14% success</strong>, not 14% direct XP. Exquisite urns return <strong>25%</strong> before enhancer; enhancer raises urn payouts <strong>25%</strong>, making that <strong>31.25%</strong> of eligible base XP.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Fishing_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfits, tools, urns and consumables</a>. Exquisite urns are not the standard cheap tradeable urn option; decorated urns plus enhancer yield <strong>25%</strong>, not 31.25%.</p>\n<p><strong>Perk maths:</strong> Furnace 4 consumes resources for double XP with <strong>20% probability</strong>, rising to <strong>22% at item level 20</strong>: +20%/+22% expected eligible catch XP. It works with shark outfit consumption but does not stack normally with Crystallise. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Furnace_(perk)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Furnace</a></p>\n<p><strong>Additional options:</strong> Fishing accumulators award <strong>2,500 XP</strong> when charged by failed attempts; assess their GP/XP. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Fishing_accumulator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Accumulator</a>. Deep Sea Fishing&#x27;s tangled fishbowl provides temporary <strong>5% XP</strong>; its catch boosts are separate. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Deep_Sea_Fishing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hub boosts</a></p>\n<p><strong>Limits:</strong> bonuses vary by spot; do not multiply every listed percentage into a universal XP multiplier. Fish-farm mechanics merit a separate test. Bait and Switch primarily adds Cooking XP, while porters primarily save banking time. Legacy Call of the Sea aura recommendations are obsolete after the April aura overhaul. Do not build a long-term plan around soon-to-be-removed dwarven extractors/cores.</p>"},{"id":"hunter","name":"Hunter","category":"Gathering","icon":"trap","summary":"One kit never fits every creature. Build for trapping, moths or big-game hunts.","bonus":"Outfit + yaktwee: +8% XP","tiers":{"low":["Enhanced yaktwee stick","Decorated Hunter urns","Hunter cape"],"medium":["Hunter’s outfit / trapper set","Extreme Hunter potions","Urn enhancer"],"high":["Volcanic trapper outfit","Skeka’s hypnowand where useful","Tellervo tools for moths"]},"caution":"Tools can compete for the same slots","notes":"<p><strong>Best equipment depends on the creature: one universal loadout would be misleading.</strong> Hunter now extends to 110; the general training guide explicitly warns its method rankings may lag Havenhythe.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Recommended equipment and effect</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Enhanced yaktwee stick: <strong>+2% Hunter XP</strong>, earned by catching 1,000 charm sprites. Decorated Hunter urns provide <strong>20% of eligible base training XP</strong>. Hunter cape activation instantly deploys a trap.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Own the complete Hunter’s outfit: <strong>+6% XP</strong>; obtain it from Waiko. A complete desert/jungle/arctic trapper set inherits that XP bonus and adds <strong>5% catch success</strong>. Add extreme Hunter potions, a familiar, and an urn enhancer.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Volcanic trapper outfit inherits the owned +6% outfit and provides <strong>7% success</strong>, a sixth trap, 30% instant deployment/pickup, and 10% double catches with extra XP (not Big Game Hunter/divine locations). Use Skeka’s hypnowand for appropriate methods; Tellervo equipment for moths.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Hunter_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Equipment and training mechanics</a></p>\n<p><strong>Stack correctly:</strong> outfit 6% + enhanced stick 2% = <strong>8% additive XP</strong>, not 11% from obsolete guides. An urn enhancer multiplies the urn payout by 1.25: decorated urns contribute 25% of eligible base XP; exquisite contribute 31.25%, rather than adding 25 percentage points. Exquisite Hunter urns require <strong>109 Crafting to activate</strong>, so all-99 does not yet satisfy that gate. Urns and effigies cannot fill together. Brawling gloves replace an outfit piece; do not count both complete outfits simultaneously. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">XP stacking</a></p>\n<p><strong>Throughput is separate:</strong> Skeka’s off-hand gives 20% faster BGH construction/arming, more multi-dinosaur encounters, and trapping benefits—not flat +20% XP. Buying it requires 80 Hunter; self-restoration requires 103 Archaeology. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Skeka%27s_hypnowand\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Skeka</a></p>\n<p>For moths, Tellervo’s net improves catches and its lantern prevents fleeing and attracts/automatically catches eligible moths; neither replaces the fungal-spore tool at Croesus. These occupy slots otherwise used by the stick/Skeka. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Tellervo%27s_net\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Net</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Tellervo%27s_lantern\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lantern</a></p>\n<p>Avoid obsolete tracker-aura recommendations. Do not treat November preview changes as live or promise a universal maximum XP/hour from unverified new-method rankings.</p>"},{"id":"mining","name":"Mining","category":"Gathering","icon":"pickaxe","summary":"Match your pickaxe and perks to the rock, your stamina and your attention.","bonus":"Golden mining suit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Elder rune pickaxe +5","Golden mining suit","Decorated Mining urns"],"medium":["Pickaxe of earth and song","Magic golem outfit","Perfect juju & stone spirits"],"high":["Pickaxe of life and death","Tagga’s corehammer","Gargoyle & rockertunity tools"]},"caution":"Life and death requires 100 Mining","notes":"<p><strong>Priority:</strong> buy inexpensive XP support first; expensive equipment improves mining damage rather than applying one universal XP multiplier.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and supplies</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Elder rune pickaxe +5 at 99; golden mining suit if unlocked; decorated Mining urns; ore box; lava titan; maintain stamina and click rockertunities.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Augmented pickaxe of earth and song; Furnace 4 for ordinary mining XP; magic golem outfit inheriting golden suit; urn enhancer; ring of whispers; perfect juju mining potion with matching stone spirits for AFK core ores.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>At <strong>100 Mining</strong>, augmented pickaxe of life and death; Tagga’s corehammer; gargoyle familiar with Hammer Rock scrolls; superior rock-crushing scrimshaw; powerburst of opportunity on rockertunities. Grace of the elves/porters reduce banking.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Direct XP:</strong> golden mining suit provides <strong>6%</strong> in full. Urns yield <strong>20% of eligible base XP</strong>; enhancer increases the urn reward by 25%, making that component <strong>25% of base</strong>, not 45%. Furnace 4 has a 20% activation chance for doubled XP without progress; it sacrifices gathering progress and does <strong>not</strong> combine with Crystallise. Wise 4 on an off-hand is an alternative while not wielding Tagga. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Mining_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and equipment</a></p>\n<p><strong>Active alternative:</strong> Crystallise + Light Form gives <strong>40% extra XP</strong> at eligible core rocks while forfeiting resources; it does not work at Seren stones or alaea crablets. Use a different perk setup from Furnace. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Crystallise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spell restrictions</a></p>\n<p><strong>Damage/support:</strong> gargoyle adds <strong>12 damage per swing</strong>, and its scroll makes the next swing deal <strong>50% more</strong>—particularly useful with rockertunities. These are not flat 12%/50% hourly XP multipliers. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Gargoyle_(familiar)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Familiar</a></p>\n<p>Life and death requires <strong>100 Mining</strong>, quest/achievement unlocks and 100 Smithing (Smithing boostable); primal +5 is a cheaper unaugmentable level-100 alternative. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pickaxe_of_life_and_death\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pickaxe requirements</a></p>\n<p><strong>Cautions:</strong> bracelet of clay is a clay-yield tool, not a general Mining XP upgrade. Do not recommend removed Quarrymaster auras; legacy dwarven-tool/core boosts are temporary pending 23 November removal. Exact best perks vary between core ores, Crystallise and non-core AFK methods; no universal multiplied total is justified.</p>"},{"id":"woodcutting","name":"Woodcutting","category":"Gathering","icon":"axe","summary":"A better hatchet helps. Perks, tree choice and banking determine the rest.","bonus":"Lumberjack outfit: +5% XP","tiers":{"low":["Owned augmentable hatchet","Lumberjack outfit","Woodcutting urns"],"medium":["Hatchet of ember and glade","Nature’s sentinel outfit","Urn enhancer"],"high":["Hatchet of bloom and blight","Sana’s fyrtorch","Method-specific modern perks"]},"caution":"Bloom and blight requires level 100","notes":"<h3>Woodcutting — equipment and XP boosts (checked 2 November 2026)</h3>\n<p><strong>At 99:</strong> prioritise an augmented <strong>hatchet of ember and glade</strong>; it requires 90 Woodcutting/Attack, 90 Smithing and substantial quest unlocks. <strong>Hatchet of bloom and blight requires 100 Woodcutting</strong>, so belongs to your next-level plan. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Hatchet_of_ember_and_glade\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hatchet requirements</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Recommended package</th><th>What improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low cost</td><td>Owned augmented crystal/imcando hatchet, affordable Honed perks, Lumberjack outfit, decorated Woodcutting urns, beaver, perfect juju Woodcutting potion</td><td>XP per action plus more successful cuts</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Ember and glade, Honed 6, Nature’s sentinel outfit with Lumberjack bonus unlocked, Ring of Whispers, urn enhancer; log-splitting scrimshaw where worthwhile</td><td>Strong practical upgrade without buying every luxury</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Same hatchet at 99; bloom and blight at 100; Sana’s fyrtorch, method-appropriate high-end perks, superior log-splitting scrimshaw, continual potion/urn supply</td><td>Maximum throughput and extra XP-producing logs; ongoing charges/consumables</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Direct XP:</strong> Lumberjack provides <strong>5%</strong>; Nature’s sentinel can retain its unlocked bonus. Urns award <strong>20% of eligible filling XP</strong>; enhancer increases urn rewards 25%, making the urn contribution <strong>25%, not 45%</strong>. Crystallise supplies <strong>20%</strong>, or <strong>40% with Light Form</strong>, sacrificing logs; it <strong>does not stack with Furnace</strong>. Old 87.5% claims are obsolete. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience-boosting_sets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit bonuses</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Urns\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Urns</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Crystallise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crystallise</a></p>\n<p><strong>Throughput:</strong> Honed 6 improves gathering chance; Sana’s fyrtorch gives +6% success chance and 20% chance of an extra XP-bearing log; perfect juju gives 5% double logs. Beaver supplies +2 invisible levels. These are not interchangeable flat XP multipliers. Naturalist versus Furnace is method-dependent: current perk guidance recommends Furnace 4/Wise 2 over Naturalist 3 only at approximately 23% success or less. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Optimal_skilling_perk_setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Current perk comparison</a></p>\n<p><strong>Training choice:</strong> golden bamboo is available now; include island-search time when comparing rates. Eternal magic trees unlock at 100. Wood boxes, porters and Always Adze reduce banking; Brooch storage/nests primarily add convenience or loot. Do not automatically multiply every bonus together. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Woodcutting_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and consumable details</a></p>\n<p><strong>Uncertainties:</strong> no personally measured XP/hour or live purchase prices; optimal perks depend on target tree. Exclude obsolete lumberjack-aura recommendations and treat planned November removals separately from live equipment.</p>"},{"id":"construction","name":"Construction","category":"Artisan","icon":"hammer","summary":"Build with the current system. Contracts and Fort projects need different kits.","bonus":"Constructor outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Construction cape","Constructor outfit pieces","Plank box & saving scroll"],"medium":["Master constructor outfit","Sculpting chisel","Upgraded plank box"],"high":["Artificer’s measure","Eternal-plank contracts at 100","Furniture depacker at 109 Invention"]},"caution":"Old build/remove loops were reworked","notes":"<p>Construction now extends to <strong>120</strong>. The July rework replaced the old build/remove hotspot loop with furniture production at workbenches. Old portable-workbench advice is unreliable: the launch disabled those workbenches; do not buy one expecting its historical 10% boost. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Update:Player_Owned_Housing_Rework_Out_Now%21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official launch</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Player-owned_house\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">current house system</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>What actually improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Construction cape; owned Constructor pieces; plank box and Scroll of Proficiency</td><td>Cape saves 5% of planks; scroll saves eligible planks. These reduce cost, rather than multiply displayed XP. Full Constructor outfit gives 6% XP.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Master constructor outfit, with ordinary outfit owned; sculpting chisel; upgraded plank box</td><td>Master outfit inherits the owned 6%, rather than stacking a second outfit bonus; boosts contract progress and offers direct teleports. Chisel adds 1% XP.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Artificer&#x27;s measure; highest unlocked furniture or eternal-plank contracts; furniture depacker later</td><td>Measure builds a conditional buff up to 5% XP through Scroll of Proficiency activations. Depacker is automation, not an XP multiplier.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>The <strong>Artificer&#x27;s measure requires 99 Crafting and 102 Archaeology to create, both boostable</strong>; all-99 does not automatically satisfy its unboosted requirements. It multiplies scroll activation chance by 1.25, not total Construction XP by 1.25. Each activation gives 0.5% XP for five minutes, up to ten stacks. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Artificer%27s_measure\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Measure</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Method choice:</strong> eternal-plank contracts start at 100 Construction; the training guide lists approximately 1.56m XP/hour with the master outfit, an estimate rather than guaranteed performance. Fort reinforcement remains the AFK alternative. Its own optimal-hotspot mechanic can add up to 60% XP per project and 40% build speed; Fort Workshop boosts apply locally, not to all furniture production. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Construction_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training guide</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Stacking:</strong> add relevant generic boosts, but never multiply every percentage together. Wise occupies an augmented weapon slot; the chisel is not augmentable, so choose compatible slots. The chisel comes from four qualifying monthly God Statue completions; the statues&#x27; own XP excludes outfit/chisel/bonus XP. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/God_Statues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">God Statues</a>. Furniture depacker requires <strong>109 Invention</strong>, beyond the stated all-99 account. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Devices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devices</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Uncertainty:</strong> the training guide explicitly warns of post-rework outdated material. Verify any portable functionality in-game; omit removed functional auras and treat pre-23-November consumable boosts as temporary, not permanent equipment.</p>"},{"id":"cooking","name":"Cooking","category":"Artisan","icon":"cook","summary":"Prevent burns, use the right kitchen, and let urns reward every batch.","bonus":"Sous chef outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Cooking cape","Owned sous chef pieces","Suitable range or fire"],"medium":["Full sous chef outfit","Tier-3 Fort Kitchen","Urns & enhancer"],"high":["Highest usable urns","Optimised bank presets","Premium recipe if affordable"]},"caution":"No-burn effects are not flat XP bonuses","notes":"<h3>Cooking — researched 2 November 2026</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and setup</th><th>What improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Cooking cape; bank preset; decorated cooking urns; use an existing communal portable range while still live</td><td>Cape prevents burning, protecting XP/materials; decorated urns add 20% of eligible base Cooking XP. Cape is not an XP multiplier.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full sous chef outfit; Fort Forinthry tier-3 Kitchen; urn enhancer</td><td>Outfit gives 6% Cooking XP; Kitchen increases base Cooking XP 5%; enhancer multiplies urn reward by 1.25, turning decorated urn contribution into 25% of eligible base XP.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Medium setup plus exquisite cooking urns where obtainable/usable; modified toque; Inspire Genius relic; fast bank-adjacent cooking, optionally manual two-tick cooking</td><td>Exquisite urn reward is 3,509.4 with enhancer per 11,230 fill XP: approximately 31.25% eligible base XP, not 31.25% of already boosted XP. Modified toque extra-food proc improves output, not an additional XP multiplier. Inspire Genius adds 2% artisan XP.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>At all-99, Cooking cape is the straightforward no-burn solution. Cooking gauntlets can retain the sous-chef mitts XP and full-set bonus if those mitts are owned; do not add another 1% for wearing both. Gloves reduce burning, while cape prevents it. Exquisite urn creation AND rune activation require 103 Crafting: the user cannot personally activate these at unboosted 99; decorated urns are the immediate practical choice.</p>\n<p>Current portable range reports up to 21% base XP and 5% extra food. This is temporary: portables are scheduled for removal on November 23; see the shared transition notes. Do not multiply together every listed bonus: outfit/relic/general boosts and urn XP use different bases. No verified Cooking-specific augmented tool/off-hand multiplier found; avoid buying generic expensive tools for this skill. Cooking beyond 99 remains virtual progression, not newly unlocked food tiers.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Cooking_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Cooking_gauntlets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gauntlets and outfit interaction</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Exquisite_cooking_urn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">exquisite urn thresholds/reward</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Fort_Forinthry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fort Kitchen</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Portable_range\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">portable</a>.</p>"},{"id":"crafting","name":"Crafting","category":"Artisan","icon":"gem","summary":"Preserve materials or spend for speed. Your recipe decides the best accessory.","bonus":"Artisan outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Crafting cape","Basic chisel","Fast bank preset"],"medium":["Full Artisan’s outfit","Scroll of dexterity","Recipe-specific supplies"],"high":["Artificer’s measure","Crystal chisel for gems","Offering amulet for output sacrifice"]},"caution":"Artificer’s measure needs 102 Archaeology","notes":"<p><strong>Best practical purchase order:</strong> Crafting cape → Artisan&#x27;s outfit → scroll of dexterity for leather methods → Artificer&#x27;s measure once Archaeology permits. Buy expensive accessories only after selecting your training method.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>What actually improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Crafting cape (99,000 GP); bank preset; basic chisel; use an existing public portable crafter while still available</td><td>Cape supplies thread and has a <strong>0.75% chance to cut the remaining inventory of matching gems instantly</strong>. This is throughput, not an XP multiplier.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full <strong>Artisan&#x27;s outfit</strong>, earned through Stealing Creation; scroll of dexterity for leather production</td><td>Outfit gives <strong>6% direct XP</strong>. Scroll saves leather on eligible multi-hide items: savings rather than extra XP per item.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td><strong>Artificer&#x27;s measure</strong> off-hand; Brooch of the Gods for portable-compatible training; crystal chisel for gem-cutting</td><td>Measure builds <strong>0.5% XP per qualifying scroll activation, up to 5% for five minutes</strong>. Crafting it requires <strong>99 Crafting and 102 Archaeology</strong>, so all-99 does not satisfy the latter requirement. Brooch improves material retention; crystal chisel&#x27;s <strong>2% extra-gem chance</strong> improves output, not automatically XP.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Artisan%27s_outfit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Artificer%27s_measure\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Measure</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Crafting_cape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cape</a></p>\n<p>For speed, compare dragonstone cutting and dragonhide bodies at current net GP/XP. For longer production batches, consider upgraded armour/adorning and exquisite urn manufacture as higher levels unlock. <strong>There is no Crafting urn that fills while training Crafting</strong>: manufacturing urns earns Crafting XP, but their eventual contents reward other skills. Amulet of Artisan&#x27;s Offerings adds <strong>10% XP while destroying the output</strong>—an expensive optional speed choice, not a free upgrade. The amulet of the expert instead improves adorning progress; progress is not a universal XP multiplier.</p>\n<p><strong>Date-sensitive:</strong> portable crafters currently give <strong>10% XP</strong> on eligible actions; brooch retention bonuses are not an additional XP multiplier. Portables are scheduled for removal <strong>23 November</strong>. Future brooch scroll-proc changes remain proposals. Do not combine all percentages into a blanket multiplicative total: method eligibility, conditional stacks, bonus XP and DXP follow separate rules. No retired skilling aura is included.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Crafting_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and bonuses</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Latent_Offering\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Offering amulet</a> · <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/110-crafting---new-skilling-update\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">110 Crafting</a></p>"},{"id":"firemaking","name":"Firemaking","category":"Artisan","icon":"flame","summary":"Balance log cost, burn speed and the bonus from each eligible action.","bonus":"Ring + flame gloves: +5% XP","tiers":{"low":["Ring of fire","Flame gloves","Affordable bonfire logs"],"medium":["Augmented crystal tinderbox","Tinker & Pyromaniac perks","Reborn phoenix"],"high":["Premium perk combinations","Charged pitch can","Conditional Orthen furnace core"]},"caution":"Pitch can needs refilling","notes":"<p>At 99, prioritise bonfire throughput before expensive marginal equipment. No above-99 Firemaking gate is needed for this setup.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and method</th><th>Benefit</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Shared portable brazier; ring of fire and flame gloves from All Fired Up; affordable logs</td><td>Brazier gives 10% base XP plus the five-person bonfire bonus, reported as 14.4% total. Ring/gloves give 2% individually or 5% together—not 4%.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Augmented crystal tinderbox or pyro-matic, Tinker 4 and Pyromaniac 6; reborn phoenix</td><td>Tinker 4 averages 5% extra XP on eligible actions (20% chance × 25% extra). Phoenix has a 7% chance to burn two logs. Use magic/elder logs according to current cost per XP.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Above plus Pyromaniac 6/Rapid 2 combination gizmo; charged pitch can; consider Orthen furnace core</td><td>Pitch can reduces bonfire interval from six to five ticks: 20% more actions before banking. Rapid increases throughput; Pyromaniac burns the remaining matching logs on a proc.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Firemaking_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and equipment</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Optimal_skilling_perk_setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Perk configurations</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pitch_can\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pitch can</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Important expensive-item caveat:</strong> Orthen furnace core needs 99 Smithing and 102 Archaeology to make (boostable). Its Pyromaniac-triggered 5% XP buff lasts five minutes; it is not permanent 5%. Its replacement forge phoenixes can reduce XP if you actively collect normal fire spirits, so it is not universally best. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Orthen_furnace_core\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Core mechanics</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Stacking:</strong> add maximum-potency torstol incense (+2% base XP); treat direct XP, extra-log procs and action-speed gains separately rather than adding everything into one percentage. Pitch-can refill time and banking reduce the practical 20% speed gain. <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=itemdb_rs/Torstol+incense+sticks/viewitem?obj=47715\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official torstol description</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope limits:</strong> these bonfire perks are not automatically applicable to incense production or zygomite hair-burning. Incense crafting can preserve money but is slower. Do not recommend removed auras. Future MTX changes should not be treated as already live. No audited universal maximum stack or live consumable prices established.</p>"},{"id":"fletching","name":"Fletching","category":"Artisan","icon":"feather","summary":"Find the balance between fast XP, saved materials and a saleable finished item.","bonus":"Fletcher outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Fletching cape","Owned Fletcher outfit pieces","Tier-3 Ranger’s Workroom"],"medium":["Amulet of Offerings","Wise 4 off-hand","Fenshell knife where applicable"],"high":["Method-specific amulet","Premium training supplies","Scripture or pocket choice"]},"caution":"Martial training destroys its output","notes":"<p><strong>Low:</strong> wear the Fletching cape (99; 0.75% chance of extra ammunition <strong>with XP</strong>), use owned Fletcher’s outfit pieces (1% each, full five-piece set <strong>6%</strong>), and train at the tier-3 Ranger’s Workroom (<strong>5% base XP</strong>, plus tier-2 1% extra-ammunition proc). Obtain outfit through Stealing Creation/Thaler/merchant routes. These are priority unlocks rather than a reason to buy expensive consumables. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience-boosting_sets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Cape_of_Accomplishment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cape</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Ranger%27s_Workroom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">workroom</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Medium:</strong> add <strong>Amulet of Offerings</strong>, from *Ode of the Devourer*: <strong>3% Fletching XP</strong>, stacking with the outfit. Use a Wise 4 augmented off-hand (<strong>4%</strong>, capped at 50,000 extra XP/day). Choose a <strong>Fenshell knife</strong> for applicable ordinary production: <strong>7% resource-saving</strong>, not 7% XP; for Fenmoor Totems its one-tick faster actions improve throughput. It cannot be augmented. Crystal knife remains specifically useful for Zygomite Carestyling: 5% double shafts <strong>and XP</strong>, without degrading there. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Fletching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fletching equipment</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Fenshell_knife\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">knife</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Fletching_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">carestyling/boosts</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>High:</strong> optimise the chosen method, not merely item price. <strong>Amulet of Fletcher’s Offerings</strong> gives <strong>10% extra base XP but destroys finished products</strong>, replacing the neck-slot 3% amulet; <strong>Amulet of the expert</strong> gives <strong>20% extra progress/action for martial equipment</strong>, not a blanket 20% XP multiplier. Scripture of Elidinis adds collectible-soul XP, competing with Brooch in pocket. Brooch currently doubles portable proc chances: useful resource savings, not double XP. Full-priced darts/martial output destruction can heavily lose money. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Fletching_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Method-specific equipment</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Brooch_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brooch</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Timing/uncertainty:</strong> portable fletcher currently gives <strong>10% base XP</strong>; portables/cores are scheduled for removal <strong>23 November</strong>. The <strong>30 October proposal</strong> replaces Brooch’s portable interaction with +5 percentage points to specified Dungeoneering scroll procs; it is not live and adds no blanket Fletching XP. Do not buy Brooch solely for expiring portable synergy. Generic bonuses usually add; base-XP bonuses can multiply generic bonuses. Training-guide XP/hour figures explicitly warn of outdated 2026 tiers; Fenshell applicability to martial/masterwork and bakriminel actions remains uncertain. <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/whats-happening-with-mtx-items-in-runescape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Removal</a>, <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/late-game-rebalance-design-preview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">latest proposal</a>.</p>"},{"id":"herblore","name":"Herblore","category":"Artisan","icon":"potion","summary":"XP gear and potion-saving gear solve different problems. Choose intentionally.","bonus":"Botanist outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Owned Botanist pieces","Scroll of cleansing","Bank preset & recipe plan"],"medium":["Full Botanist outfit","Modified botanist mask","Method-specific Factory pieces"],"high":["High-level recipe unlocks","Owned useful accessories","Premium supplies by GP/XP"]},"caution":"Extra potions do not automatically give XP","notes":"<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> full Botanist for maximum XP; sacrifice three pieces for Factory only when cheaper potion output matters more than XP. Herblore has no conventional augmented training tool: use a Wise off-hand for its daily-limited XP benefit instead.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>Actual benefit</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Bank preset; public portable well; Scroll of cleansing (20,000 Dungeoneering tokens)</td><td>Well: +10% XP and 5% duplicate chance. Scroll: 10% ingredient saving and 12.5% chance to shorten the next potion by one tick; saving and throughput, not an XP multiplier.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full Botanist outfit, including modified mask; Wise equipment; perfect juju Herblore for combination potions</td><td>Outfit +6% XP. Mask adds 5% duplicate chance; duplicates award no XP. Perfect juju adds 5% XP specifically for six-dose combinations.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Above plus Brooch of the Gods; relevant recipe unlocks; optional Scripture of Elidinis</td><td>Currently Brooch doubles the well&#x27;s duplication chance to 10%; it does not double XP. Scripture supplies separate additional XP, with page costs.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Herblore_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training equipment and method overview</a>. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scroll_of_cleansing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Scroll mechanics</a>. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Modified_botanist%27s_mask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modified mask</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Specialisation:</strong> Three Factory pieces replace three Botanist pieces: retain modified mask, but lose the full-set XP bonus. Factory and Botanist&#x27;s amulets increase eligible potion doses rather than XP. Meilyr Voice of Seren gives +20% XP on combinations made there. Recipe unlocks remain necessary. Level boosts cannot unlock improved higher-level powerburst recipes.</p>\n<p><strong>Above 99:</strong> the <strong>120 Herblore master cape</strong> unlocks five overloads/elder overloads for four sets, or four supremes for three. This is ingredient efficiency, not free proportional XP: batch XP/time follow ingredients consumed. Ordinary 99 cape herb cleaning grants <strong>no XP</strong>. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Herblore_master_cape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cape details</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Imminent change:</strong> portable wells and cores are due for removal 23 November. Do not buy an expensive Brooch solely for today&#x27;s portable effect. The late-November proposal replaces that benefit with <strong>+5 percentage points to Dungeoneering-scroll proc chances</strong>; final implementation is unconfirmed. <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/late-game-rebalance-design-preview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official preview</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Stacking limitation:</strong> do not multiply every percentage together or count duplicate potions as XP; consult the general XP-stack section for outfit/bonus-XP/event rules. Potion-specific exceptions and workbench services must be checked against the chosen recipe.</p>"},{"id":"runecrafting","name":"Runecrafting","category":"Artisan","icon":"rune","summary":"Craft smarter: XP bonuses and extra rune output are not the same thing.","bonus":"Master runecrafter robes: +5%","tiers":{"low":["Master runecrafter robes","Essence pouches","Decorated Runecrafting urns"],"medium":["Infinity ethereal outfit","Abyssal titan","Urn enhancer & fast teleports"],"high":["Runic attuner for standard altars","Expansive pouch at actual 105","Optimised soul-altar route"]},"caution":"Demonic skull no longer boosts RC XP","notes":"<p><strong>Best investment order at 99:</strong> Master runecrafter XP outfit → urns/enhancer → essence capacity and movement → Runic attuner if training traditional altars. Necrotic runes are a separate profit-friendly route; the attuner excludes their altars.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and training package</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Master runecrafter robes: full set <strong>+5% XP</strong>. Carry decorated Runecrafting urns; all five available essence pouches increase XP per trip. At 99 all these pouches are usable. Pouch Protector relic prevents degradation; fast bank presets and teleports matter more than expensive jewellery.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Infinity ethereal outfit inherits owned master robes’ XP bonus and stores <strong>12 essence</strong>; abyssal titan holds <strong>20</strong> (93 Summoning). Add urn enhancer. Passing bracelet&#x27;s Haunt on the Hill teleport improves necrotic-rune trips, rather than multiplying XP.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Runic attuner: <strong>+50% additional XP at its attuned altar</strong>, rising to <strong>+2,200% on every 50th craft</strong>; target a fully charged soul altar for that craft (Menaphos soul-altar quest access required). Upgrade to <strong>70-essence expansive pouch at actual 105 Runecrafting</strong>, replacing the other pouches; cannot boost the Runecrafting requirement.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Major outdated-advice trap:</strong> Since 29 September 2025, neither the Abyss nor Demonic skull grants Runecrafting XP bonuses. The level-based Savvy Runecrafting benefit replaces them, reaching <strong>+300% at 105</strong>. Do not opt into PvP for an obsolete XP bonus. <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/amascut-combat-masteries--qol-runecrafting---this-week-in-runescape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official changes</a></p>\n<p><strong>XP versus output:</strong> Multiple runes per essence, Ring of Imbuing, cape anima-stone effect and crystal binding rod’s +5% rune yield are primarily output/profit benefits; more runes do not ordinarily mean more XP. Rod perks can change rune types: avoid their activation on the attuner’s important soul craft. Wise can supply limited extra XP; Enlightened affects <strong>Invention item XP</strong>, not Runecrafting XP.</p>\n<p>Urns up to decorated provide an effective <strong>20%</strong> extra XP on qualifying filling XP; exquisite provide <strong>25%</strong>, and enhancer increases urn rewards by <strong>25%</strong>, not all training XP. Do not multiply every bonus together indiscriminately.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Runecrafting_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training equipment</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Runic_attuner\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">attuner mechanics</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Expansive_pouch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">expansive pouch requirements</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_binding_rod\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">crystal binding rod</a>.</p>\n<p>Uncertainty: source snippets disagree about exquisite urn manufacture/use levels; verify its current item requirement before buying. No aura recommendation: functional auras were removed in April 2026. Do not budget around paid XP supplies ahead of the announced November transition.</p>"},{"id":"smithing","name":"Smithing","category":"Artisan","icon":"anvil","summary":"Keep the heat high and the progress moving. Burial is speed at a material cost.","bonus":"Blacksmith outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Smithing cape","Blacksmith outfit pieces","Perfect juju Smithing potion"],"medium":["Full blacksmith outfit","Augmented crystal hammer","Autoheater & Superheat Form"],"high":["Careless 5 + Rapid 4","Powerburst of masterstroke","Amulet of the expert for burial"]},"caution":"Primal burial starts at level 100","notes":"<p><strong>Recommendation at 99:</strong> buy elder-rune +5 burial sets for speed; switch to <strong>primal burial sets at 100</strong>. Burial consumes the equipment, so this is a spending method, not a profit method. Smithing currently has a real 110 cap. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Smithing_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training and boosts</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and consumables</th><th>What it improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Smithing cape; available blacksmith outfit pieces; perfect juju Smithing potion; smithing urns; train inside Artisans’ Workshop with a luminite injector active</td><td>Cape gives +5 base progress on the strike after reheating. Juju gives 5% double-progress chance. Outfit is direct XP; injector is +1 progress per strike.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full blacksmith outfit; augmented crystal hammer with affordable Rapid/Tinker ranks; advanced autoheater; Superheat Form; urn enhancer</td><td>Full outfit gives <strong>6% direct XP</strong>, not 6% per piece. Crystal hammer has 1% double-progress chance. Heat tools principally improve throughput and attention requirements.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Augmented crystal hammer with <strong>Careless 5 + Rapid 4</strong> for active reheating; powerburst of masterstroke; amulet of the expert for burial; Orthen furnace core; best available smithing urns with enhancer</td><td>Careless raises base progress 50% but consumes extra heat; Rapid 4 gives 20% double-progress chance and extra heat loss. Masterstroke makes the next four swings 10× progress, within 30 seconds, on a two-minute cooldown.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>The amulet adds 20% burial progress and has 250 charges. <strong>Do not call masterstroke “10× hourly XP”</strong>: only four swings qualify. Enhanced hammer-tron mainly improves Invention item XP; crystal hammer retains its Smithing progress benefit. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Enhanced_hammer-tron\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hammer comparison</a></p>\n<p>Orthen core creation requires <strong>99 Smithing and 102 Archaeology, boostable</strong>. It removes Superheat Form’s prayer drain. Its <strong>5% XP buff requires a Breakdown activation</strong>, lasts five minutes, and is not permanent. A Breakdown-containing alternative sacrifices optimal progress perks; current training advice includes Careless, while the core page’s older perk recommendation still lists Tinker/Rapid. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Orthen_furnace_core\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Core and conditions</a></p>\n<p><strong>Stacking:</strong> outfit XP, urn rewards, and progress bonuses are distinct; do not add their percentages into one multiplier. Urn enhancer increases urn payout by 25%, rather than all Smithing XP. Modified helmet’s 1% XP replaces its base helmet bonus; its additional double-bar benefit concerns smelting, not burial speed. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Modified_blacksmith%27s_helmet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Helmet</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Urn_enhancer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Urn enhancer</a></p>"},{"id":"agility","name":"Agility","category":"Support","icon":"boot","summary":"Keep moving. Lap rewards, failure prevention and XP bonuses work differently.","bonus":"Nimble outfit: +6% XP","tiers":{"low":["Agility cape","Owned Nimble pieces","Course-appropriate movement"],"medium":["Full Nimble outfit","Collector’s insignia","Anachronia spa bonus"],"high":["Best owned insignia","Efficient course route","Applicable limited boosts"]},"caution":"Silverhawks are scheduled for removal","notes":"<p><strong>Best durable active setup:</strong> full Nimble outfit, Agility cape perk, Collector’s insignia, fast movement unlocks, and the Anachronia course with its spa upgraded. There is no stronger tool unlocked by raising Agility above 99; extra levels are virtual.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>What improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Agility cape; available Nimble pieces; Surge and Dive; weight at or below zero where practical</td><td>Cape prevents obstacle failures; each Nimble piece adds 1% XP, full set 6%. Movement reduces travel time.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full Nimble; Double Surge; Mobile on augmented equipment; Collector’s insignia; tier 1–2 Anachronia spa</td><td>Insignia gives 5% extra course-lap XP; spa increases Anachronia base XP by 5%/7%.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Above plus charged Collector’s insignia; tier 3 spa; Inspire Love relic; Torstol incense; clan boost</td><td>Insignia rises to 10% on eligible lap rewards; spa 10%; relic 2%; incense up to 2%; clan up to 6%.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Anachronia timing matters:</strong> Roar of Osseous adds 25% XP during its window. Practised Surge/Dive routes improve XP/hour without multiplying each obstacle’s XP. Mobile and Shadow’s Grace are alternative cooldown solutions, not independent multipliers to add together. At 99, the cape makes failure-prevention incense redundant. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Agility_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training mechanics</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Anachronia_base_camp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">spa tiers</a>, <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Experience-boosting_sets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">outfit and insignia limits</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Do not sum everything into one universal multiplier:</strong> insignia applies to course/lap rewards, spa to Anachronia, and movement to throughput. Inspire Love requires <strong>116 Archaeology</strong>, so it is not immediately available with all skills at 99. A charged insignia also entails Barbarian Assault unlocks and upkeep.</p>\n<p><strong>Temporary, November 2 only:</strong> Silverhawk boots supply separate passive XP rather than multiplying course XP; they can preserve the Nimble bonus when Nimble boots are owned. Silverhawks and XP cores are scheduled for removal <strong>November 23, 2026</strong>. Do not build a durable setup around them or obsolete Surefooted-aura advice. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/2026_microtransaction_items_changes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Removal schedule</a>.</p>\n<p>Uncertainty: exact combined stacking and attainable laps/hour depend on reward component and route execution; no single maximum percentage or guaranteed rate is claimed.</p>"},{"id":"dungeoneering","name":"Dungeoneering","category":"Support","icon":"dungeon","summary":"Finish floors efficiently. The remaster changed prestige and ring upgrades.","bonus":"Warped outfit: ~14.49% floor XP","tiers":{"low":["Ring of kinship","Strong bound equipment","Perfect juju potion"],"medium":["Gorajan trailblazer outfit","Upgraded ring passives","Lock melters"],"high":["Warped gorajan outfit","Appropriate Gorajo XP cards","Optimised bound loadout"]},"caution":"Prestige was removed in May 2026","notes":"<p><strong>Priority:</strong> learn fast high-complexity floor completion, then add outfit and cards. The May 2026 remaster removed prestige: do not follow old manual-reset/rush-for-prestige instructions. Floor buffs now reward completing unticked floors within themes and reset automatically after your available floor count is completed. Large-floor XP bonuses were subsequently increased; old launch numbers are stale. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Dungeoneering_Remastered\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Current remaster summary</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and boosts</th><th>What improves</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Ring of kinship, level-99 Dungeoneering cape, strongest available bound weapons and ammunition; perfect juju Dungeoneering potion before entry</td><td>Cheap practical foundation. Potion gives 5% damage and reduces skill-door requirements by two levels, <strong>not 5% direct XP</strong>.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Full ordinary gorajan trailblazer outfit; upgraded ring passives matching your weapon; lock melters for awkward doors</td><td>Outfit&#x27;s two 5% effects multiply: <strong>1.05 × 1.05 = 1.1025</strong>, approximately <strong>10.25% floor XP</strong>. Ring and melters increase completion speed.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Warped gorajan trailblazer outfit, optimised bound loadout and ring upgrades, suitable XP Gorajo cards; skilled team if desired</td><td>Warped outfit&#x27;s two 7% effects give <strong>1.07² = 1.1449</strong>, approximately <strong>14.49% floor XP</strong>. Preening ibis gives 1.5× floor XP; thieving locust gives 2×. Do not assume every combination stacks.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Dungeoneering_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit, equipment and potion details</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Gorajo_cards\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gorajo card effects</a></p>\n<p><strong>At 99:</strong> warped floors are already unlocked (95); floor 50 is your current maximum, floor 60 requires 119. Level 120 unlocks the fifth equipment bind. Your surface Necromancy armour cannot be brought inside: build a Daemonheim-specific bound loadout. All purchased ring classes are now passive simultaneously. Solo is viable; coordinated teams can divide exploration, but compare actual floor time rather than assuming groups always win. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Dungeoneering/Level_up_table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Level gates</a> · <a href=\"https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/patch-notes-dungeoneering-remastered\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official remaster patch</a></p>\n<p><strong>Cautions:</strong> Daemonheim aura was removed April 2026; use current achievement benefits rather than buying an aura. Generic boost compatibility and card-stacking need checking against floor reward screens; no universal maximum multiplier or fixed XP/hour is defensible without floor size, completion time and card assumptions. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Daemonheim_aura_4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aura removal</a></p>"},{"id":"slayer","name":"Slayer","category":"Support","icon":"swords","summary":"Choose better tasks, collect souls and let combat equipment improve the pace.","bonus":"100 Codex souls: +5% Slayer XP","tiers":{"low":["Best owned Slayer helmet","Necromancy spectral lens","Appropriate damage perks"],"medium":["Corrupted Slayer helmet","Anachronia helmet stand","100 souls in Slayer Codex"],"high":["Premium AoE combat loadout","Optimised preferred tasks","Sacrifice only if giving up loot"]},"caution":"Scrimshaw Slayer bonus excludes DXP","notes":"<p><strong>Best permanent direct multiplier:</strong> fill the Slayer Codex with <strong>100 different souls</strong> for <strong>+5% Slayer XP</strong> (1% per 20 souls), using a Slayer helmet or its Anachronia stand effect. This is available from 99; collecting souls takes time. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Slayer_Codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Slayer Codex</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>XP benefit</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Existing T90 Necromancy weapons/First Necromancer armour; best owned Slayer helmet; ensouled spectral lens for Necromancy; aggression potion where safe; cheap suitable perks</td><td>On-task helmet increases kill speed; it is <strong>not itself +damage% Slayer XP</strong>. Start soul collection.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Corrupted Slayer helmet; tier-3 Anachronia Slayer Lodge stand; 100 Codex souls; task-specific Genocidal/Demon Slayer/Dragon Slayer/Undead Slayer perks; cannon where allowed</td><td>Corrupted helmet: <strong>+9.5% damage, +14.5% accuracy</strong> on task, including Necromancy after lens. Stand frees the head slot for power armour. Genocidal scales up to <strong>4.9% damage</strong> through a task. These improve kills/hour rather than XP/kill.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Medium package plus suitable T95+ weapons, optimised AoE setup, efficient preferred/blocked tasks; sacrifice or corruption scrimshaw when deliberately sacrificing loot</td><td>Sacrifice gives <strong>+50% Slayer XP on task</strong>, destroying most drops. Its Slayer bonus <strong>does not apply during Double XP</strong>. Superior sacrifice extends duration; it does not increase the percentage.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Corrupted_slayer_helmet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Helmet mechanics</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Genocidal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Genocidal</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Scrimshaw_of_sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sacrifice and DXP restriction</a></p>\n<p><strong>Priority:</strong> optimise tasks before buying luxury combat equipment. Prefer/extend fast AoE tasks and block slow frequent tasks; monsters must be assigned for normal Slayer XP. At 99, abyssal savages are available; beasts require 105 and lords 115. Matching <strong>special</strong> Tower contracts can improve selected tasks; a regular contract can override assignment XP, so do not substitute one casually. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Slayer_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Task planning</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Slayer_contract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Contract warning</a></p>\n<p><strong>Uncertainty:</strong> Codex page explicitly supports the stand, but older community reports dispute XP transfer; verify a measured XP drop. No obsolete auras recommended. Avoid a long-term plan relying on Slayer wildcards/cores because of their announced November 23 removal. Generic boosts belong in the shared stacking section; do not multiply every listed percentage together.</p>"},{"id":"thieving","name":"Thieving","category":"Support","icon":"hand","summary":"Steal more successfully. Faster loot does not always mean faster experience.","bonus":"Black ibis outfit: +5% XP","tiers":{"low":["Owned Black ibis pieces","Thieving cape","Crystal Mask"],"medium":["Master camouflage outfit","Crystal Mask + Light Form","Task-specific gloves"],"high":["High-level heist equipment","Method-specific success tools","Unlocked 100+ targets"]},"caution":"Sticky Fingers trades XP per theft for speed","notes":"<p><strong>At 99:</strong> choose active Vault of Hereditas heists (95+, Breaking the Seal) or lower-attention pickpocketing. Asuran Arsenal starts at 108; Thieving now genuinely extends to 120. Heist route execution and loot retained matter more than equipping pickpocket-only bonuses. <a href=\"https://www.jagex.com/news/become-a-master-thief-sneak-your-way-above-lvl-99-with-%E2%80%98heists%E2%80%99-launching-in-runescape-today\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Heist release</a></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Equipment and unlocks</th><th>Benefit</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Gloves of silence, featherfingered necklace, 99 cape; work on hard Ardougne achievements</td><td>Gloves add 5% pickpocket success; necklace avoids some failure stuns; cape notes pickpocket loot; hard achievements add 10% success globally. These improve uptime, not XP per successful theft.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Trahaearn exoskeleton (Plague’s End), ordinary pickpocketing bag, black ibis if already owned</td><td>Exoskeleton provides the gloves-equivalent effect plus failure protection; bag accepts tool perks. Black ibis gives 5% direct XP for its complete set.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Master camouflage, inherited black ibis bonus, mushroomy pickpocketing bag with Oblivious, Ring of Vitur</td><td>Master outfit inherits ibis XP after owning/wearing it once, supplies exoskeleton effects with Plague’s End, and improves stun avoidance. Vitur adds 5% success; Oblivious extends fresh-target uptime.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Master_camouflage_outfit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outfit details</a> · <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Thieving_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Equipment comparison</a></p>\n<p><strong>Highest-impact pickpocket support:</strong> Crystal Mask (90 Magic, The Light Within) adds 15% success for five minutes and resets accumulated target threat. With Light Form it is 30%, <strong>not</strong> the obsolete 50%. This is success chance, not an XP multiplier; the former Mask stun-protection effect was removed in February 2026. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_Mask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Current spell changes</a></p>\n<p><strong>Avoid false stacking:</strong> gloves/exoskeleton/camouflage do not supply three separate gloves bonuses. Master camouflage’s doubled loot grants no extra XP. Sticky Fingers accelerates attempts 3→2 ticks but reduces XP per attempt by 33%; ideal uninterrupted XP is approximately unchanged. Mushroomy bag’s 5% speed proc does <strong>not</strong> stack with Sticky Fingers. Prefer bag without Sticky Fingers when prioritising XP; test current target-specific performance. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Mushroomy_pickpocketing_bag\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bag mechanics</a></p>\n<p><strong>Uncertainty:</strong> do not apply every pickpocket boost to safecracking or heist completion XP. No universal combined multiplier is defensible across these methods. Prioritise global XP bonuses separately; ignore obsolete aura recommendations.</p>"},{"id":"invention","name":"Invention","category":"Support","icon":"cog","summary":"Augment what you already use. Item XP and siphon rewards follow their own rules.","bonus":"XP capacitor: 2× item XP","tiers":{"low":["Existing augmented equipment","Equipment siphons at level 12","Cheap items only for disassembly"],"medium":["Mechanised siphon","XP Capacitor 5000s","Level-9 siphoning for speed"],"high":["Efficient augmented AoE setup","Capacitors & premium perks","Enlightened after damage comparison"]},"caution":"DXP gives 1.5× item XP, not 2× payout","notes":"<p><strong>Best practical approach:</strong> train combat or Slayer wearing augmented weapons, body and legs; siphon the valuable equipment rather than destroying it. Invention has a true 120 cap. Your existing T90 Necromancy weapons and First Necromancer body/legs are a suitable starting platform once augmented.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><th>Budget</th><th>Equipment and training setup</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Low</td><td>Existing augmented equipment; ordinary equipment siphons at item level 12. Alternatively disassemble genuinely cheap replacements at level 10, never expensive main equipment.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Existing T90 gear, a mechanised siphon, and charged XP Capacitor 5000s when their cost is acceptable. Set siphoning to level 9 for speed.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>High</td><td>Highest-tier effective augmented combat equipment, capacitors, and optimised AoE damage; consider Enlightened 4 on dedicated training items only after comparing the lost damage perks. Expensive ancient-gizmo manufacture is a separate buyable route, not an equipment multiplier.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Multiplier:</strong> a charged capacitor doubles item-XP generation while its charge lasts; Enlightened supplies +3% item XP per rank, up to +12% on the item carrying it. Damage perks increase throughput by increasing kills, rather than multiplying the eventual XP payout. Siphoning at 9 slightly maximises XP per item XP; 12 uses fewer siphons. Disassembly payout caps at item level 10. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Invention_training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Training mechanics</a></p>\n<p><strong>Important exceptions:</strong> DXP gives 1.5× item XP and 1.5× discovery/workbench XP, not a boosted siphon/disassembly reward. Stored bonus XP can apply to the payout; normal XP boosts do not. Do not label Wise, incense or pulse effects as an automatic additional multiplier on siphons. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Invention\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Invention XP rules</a></p>\n<p><strong>One-time priority:</strong> extreme Invention potions boost 99 to 116, enabling additional blueprint discoveries; optimise each to Perfect. This is bonus discovery XP, not a permanent level or repeatable training method. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Extreme_invention\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Extreme Invention</a></p>\n<p><strong>Convenience:</strong> mechanised siphon unlocks at 77 and automatically siphons selected items at the chosen level. It saves attention, not XP. <a href=\"https://runescape.wiki/w/Mechanised_siphon\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Device</a></p>\n<p>Checked 2 November 2026. No live GE cost or universal XP/hour claim: kill speed, charges and component costs vary. Legacy aura/MTX recommendations deliberately excluded.</p>"}];
